This opt-in test module includes the real fixed T6050 DP driver source.
It substitutes PM-domain operations and explicit poll acknowledgements,
using allocated memory instead of any hardware MMIO. It tests two cycles,
four link rates, drive requests, invalid settings and timeout stopping.
It deliberately logs a timeout for the missing-acknowledgement test.
It does not test physical link training, analog behavior or optical output.

Build against a configured ARM64 kernel:
  make -C <linux-source> O=<kernel-build> ARCH=arm64 LLVM=1 M=$PWD modules

In a QEMU Linux guest with the matching kernel, load apple-tunable.ko then
apple-t6050-driver-test.ko. Require AURORA_T6050_INTEGRATED_TEST_PASS in the
kernel log; module insertion failure is a test failure. Never use this
module's model acknowledgements as evidence about physical hardware.
